# Every Secret Manager secret mounted on the Cloud Run jobs and the API service.
#
# THIS FILE IS THE SINGLE SOURCE OF TRUTH. provision.sh, deploy-api.sh and
# .github/workflows/deploy.yml all read it. Adding a secret here and pushing a
# tag is enough; there is no second list to remember.
#
# It exists because there used to be one. The list lived only in provision.sh,
# a one-shot script CI never re-runs, so three secrets added to it on 2026-08-12
# (SMTP_PORT, SMTP_STARTTLS, OPENAI_API_KEY) were never mounted by the deploy.
# Two of the resulting failures were silent until a run died:
#   - OPENAI_API_KEY missing => FallbackLLMClient.from_env() raised and took the
#     whole daily run down rather than degrading to Anthropic.
#   - INLABS_* missing on the API service => the backfill endpoint ("Run on past
#     editions") called fetch_editions with no credentials.
#
# Both the jobs and the service get the same set. The service needs INLABS_*
# because /api/watches/<id>/backfill fetches editions inline.
DATABASE_URL
SECRET_KEY
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY
OPENAI_API_KEY
RESEND_API_KEY
RESEND_FROM
SMTP_HOST
SMTP_PORT
SMTP_USER
SMTP_PASSWORD
SMTP_STARTTLS
SMTP_FROM
INLABS_USERNAME
INLABS_PASSWORD
